## How to read an ID

| Prefix | Means | Its triad lives in |
|---|---|---|
{{#repos}}| `{{prefix}}-` | work in `{{name}}` — {{what}} | `{{name}}/specs/phase-N/` |
{{/repos}}| `{{cross}}-` | cross-repo work, or the hub's own | `.claude/context/phase-<id>-<slug>/` here, with each repo's half in its own `specs/` |
| `{{decision}}-` | a decision only the owner can make | [`open-decisions.md`](open-decisions.md) |
| `{{known_issue}}-` | a known issue, tracked until fixed or accepted | [the table at the end of this file](#known-issues) |

- **Ids are never reused or renumbered.** `python tools/next_id.py <PREFIX> --show` reads every hub
  document and prints the next free one; a mention anywhere takes an id, so write `{{cross}}-<next>` in prose
  until the id is issued.
- A cross-repo item gets **one row for the item** and **a half-row per repo** it touches (`{{first_prefix}}-<n>` for the
  `{{first_prefix}}` half of `{{cross}}-<n>`, say). The half-row names the item, so the checker's R13 can find it.
- A sub-id (`{{first_prefix}}-<n>.1`) is work inserted inside an item; it is a folder `phase-<n>.1/` in that repo.
- **Never write a real id in prose that has not been issued** — this file is scanned for mentions, so an
  example number here would take that id. Write `<n>`.

## Status — the one vocabulary

| Marker | Means | Needs |
|---|---|---|
| 🔲 `Not Started` / 🔲 `INTAKE` | nothing built; `INTAKE` is a brief just filed, no triad | — |
| 📋 `Pre-specced` | triad written, work not begun | the triad on disk |
| ⏳ `In Progress` | being worked now | — |
| ⏸️ `Parked` | deliberately stopped | a `RUN-HALTED.md` in the phase saying why |
| 🚦 `Awaiting verdict` | gates measured, the owner has not ruled | a `VERDICT-DRAFT.md` with the evidence and no verdict |
| ✅ `Completed` | every box the repo owns ticked | `verification.md` fully ticked |
| 🟢 `Live` | in production and observed there | a dated production gate |
| 🟡 `Partial` | some delivered, the rest outstanding | a table saying which |
| ➖ `N/A` | genuinely nothing to do | one line saying why |
| ⛔ `Retired` | withdrawn by the owner's ruling; terminal | the ruling and its date |

**Status comes from a row's status cell**, from the first marker in it. A marker used as a bullet in
prose or in another cell proves an id exists and says nothing about its state. Not in the vocabulary:
`⬜`, `🛠️`, `🔨` — the checker's R6 fails on them outside code spans.

